---

## Example input 1

Ich möchte die Welt verändern => I want to change the world

## Expected output 1

[Ich] möchte die Welt verändern => [I] want to change the world
Ich [möchte] die Welt verändern => I [want] to change the world
Ich möchte [die Welt] verändern => I want to change [the world]
Ich möchte die Welt [verändern] => I want to [change] the world

## Example input 2

Er hat das Buch gelesen => He read the book

## Expected output 2

[Er] hat das Buch gelesen => [He] read the book
Er [hat] das Buch gelesen => He read the book # "hat" is an auxiliary, part of "hat ... gelesen" = "read"
Er hat [das Buch] gelesen => He read [the book]
Er hat das Buch [gelesen] => He [read] the book

## Example input 3

Die Kinder spielen im Garten => The children play in the garden

## Expected output 3

[Die Kinder] spielen im Garten => [The children] play in the garden
Die Kinder [spielen] im Garten => The children [play] in the garden
Die Kinder spielen [im] Garten => The children play [in the] garden # "im" = contraction of "in dem" = "in the"
Die Kinder spielen im [Garten] => The children play in the [garden]
